  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「モパネ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%A2%E3%83%91%E3%83%8D",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 107095055,
      "text": "モパネ は、 南部アフリカ原産の、マメ科ジャケツイバラ亜科樹木。乾燥した熱帯の、標高200 - 1,200メートル の地帯に植生する。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Mopane」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mopane",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1349497910,
      "text": "Colophospermum mopane, commonly called mopane, mopani, butterfly tree, turpentine tree, or balsam tree, is a tree in the legume family (Fabaceae), that grows in hot, dry, low-lying areas, 200 to 1,200 metres in elevation, in parts of Southern Africa. The tree only occurs in Africa and is the only species in genus Colophospermum. Its distinctive butterfly-shaped (bifoliate) leaf and thin kidney-shaped/nearly semi-circular seed pod make it easy to identify."
    }
  },
